  recipeId: led
  concept: "Authored objective: Protected LED Branch Current.\nAuthored requirement:
    Install 330 ohm R_LIMIT so LED branch current is 8.0-10.5 mA. current \u2265
    8 mA. current \u2264 10.5 mA. Connection pair R_LIMIT_Input and R_LIMIT_Output.
    Conduction required.\nGeneral teaching principle: An LED has a defined anode
    and cathode; correct polarity and suitable current control matter for normal
    forward operation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that
    this objective is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Protected LED Branch Current\u2019, which component,
    reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should you inspect
    first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Protected LED Branch Current\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 14, perform the objective \u2018Protected LED Branch Current\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Install 330 ohm
    R_LIMIT so LED branch current is 8.0-10.5 mA. current \u2265 8 mA. current \u2264
    10.5 mA. Connection pair R_LIMIT_Input and R_LIMIT_Output. Conduction required.\nThe
    mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
